big-i64 mod precision

Blocker: builtin `mod(big_i64, m)` loses precision through an f64 path when
the operand exceeds f64's 53-bit mantissa (~9e15): the Park-Miller update
`mod(1103515245*1406938949 + 12345, 2147483647)` returns 178065920 instead
of the exact 178066070 (re-verified at the 0.16.1 bump). UNFILED upstream
by design (no Rust-side reproducer pinned yet) — mirrors the school shell's
pinned probe of the same drift class; full entry in docs/UPSTREAM_BUGS.md
§Tracking, re-probe at any chelis release touching the i64 `mod` runtime.
This drift is why `Shoals.Rng` hand-rolls `i64_mod` (sub/mul/floor_div)
for the Sobol/xor bit walks instead of calling the builtin.
On pass: the i64 mod path was fixed — consolidate `Shoals.Rng.i64_mod`
call sites back onto the builtin `mod` (keeping the exported shim one
release for downstream compatibility), promote this probe to a real test
under tests/, and archive the UPSTREAM_BUGS entry in the same change set.
